`Object.entries(cardNamesToEncryptedCardNumberMapping)` is called on every iteration but doesn't use the iterator variable `card`. This creates a new array on each iteration, resulting in O(n*m) complexity where n is the number of assigned cards and m is the mapping size.

**Suggested fix**: Hoist `Object.entries()` outside the loop and maintain a local array that updates as new cards are added:

```typescript
// Convert to entries once before the loop
const mappingEntries = Object.entries(cardNamesToEncryptedCardNumberMapping);

for (const card of Object.values(assignedCards)) {
    if (!card?.cardName) {
        continue;
    }

    const alreadyInMapping = mappingEntries.some(([name, encrypted]) => isMatchingCard(card, encrypted, name));

    if (!alreadyInMapping) {
        const key = card.cardName;
        const value = card.encryptedCardNumber ?? card.cardName;
        cardNamesToEncryptedCardNumberMapping[key] = value;
        mappingEntries.push([key, value]); // Keep local array in sync
    }
}
```

This avoids redundant `Object.entries()` calls while maintaining the same deduplication logic.

